---
// Every term at work together, to judge a register outside a specimen: a
// productive list of runs and an expressive instrument.
---

<article class="lab-specimen" id="X4" data-lab-context="productive">
	<div class="lab-specimen__head">
		<span class="lab-id">X4</span>
		<h3 class="lab-term">A productive list of runs</h3>
		<div class="lab-actions">
			<button class="kin-button" data-size="compact" type="button" data-x4-start
				>A run starts</button
			>
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-x4-finish>It finishes</button
			>
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-x4-sample>A sample arrives</button
			>
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				popovertarget="x4-menu">Run menu</button
			>
		</div>
		<p class="lab-meaning">
			A new run appears; its edge traces while it works and closes when it ends;
			a toast confirms it and exits; a sample lands at once; a menu comes from
			its button.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="lab-columns">
		<div class="lab-col" data-kin-motion="productive">
			<p class="lab-col__label">
				Productive <span class="lab-caption"
					>CPU <strong class="x4-sample" data-x4-figure>41%</strong></span
				>
			</p>
			<ul class="lab-rows x4-runs" data-x4-runs>
				<li
					class="kin-list__item x4-run"
					style="position: relative; --kin-pattern-edge-radius: var(--kin-radius-row)"
				>
					<span
						class="kin-pattern-live-edge"
						data-edge="ready"
						aria-hidden="true"
						><span class="kin-pattern-live-edge__line"></span></span
					>
					<div class="kin-list__body">
						<p class="kin-list__title">Nightly sync</p>
						<p class="kin-list__meta">Done</p>
					</div>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<div class="lab-toasts" data-x4-toasts aria-live="polite"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="kin-popover" popover id="x4-menu" data-padding="none">
		<div class="kin-menu" role="menu" aria-label="Run">
			<button class="kin-menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button"
				>Open the log</button
			>
			<button class="kin-menu__item" role="menuitem" type="button"
				>Run again</button
			>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>

<article class="lab-specimen" id="X5" data-lab-context="expressive">
	<div class="lab-specimen__head">
		<span class="lab-id">X5</span>
		<h3 class="lab-term">An expressive instrument</h3>
		<div class="lab-actions">
			<button class="kin-button" data-size="compact" type="button" data-x5-sight
				>First sight</button
			>
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-x5-reading>A new reading</button
			>
		</div>
		<p class="lab-meaning">
			First seen, its trace draws and its marks grow in turn; a new reading's
			figure changes at once while its needle settles, and its words arrive
			afresh.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="lab-columns">
		<div class="lab-col" data-kin-motion="expressive">
			<div class="lab-stage">
				<div class="lab-dial" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="lab-dial__hand" data-x5-hand></span>
				</div>
				<p class="lab-figure" data-x5-figure>12.4 ns</p>
				<p class="lab-reading-line" data-x5-line>
					Kepler leads the pulse by 12.4 ns.
				</p>
			</div>
			<svg class="lab-trace" viewBox="0 0 200 80" aria-hidden="true">
				<path
					d="M0 50 C 25 44 35 30 60 34 S 95 62 120 46 S 160 18 200 26"
					pathLength="1"
					data-lab-drawn></path>
			</svg>
			<div class="lab-marks" data-x5-marks>
				{
					Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, index) => (
						<span class="lab-mark" style={`--lab-i: ${index}`} />
					))
				}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>
